	source SOURCE1 {
		title.value """
Everything You Every Wanted to Know about GEDCOM Tags, But Were Afraid to Ask!
You can start new lines in this field too."""
		title {
			type abbreviated
			value All About GEDCOM Tags
		}
		author.text """
Author or Authorss of this Source using multiple lines if necessary.
Here is a new line in this field"""
		author.text Responsible agency for data in this source
		publisher """
Details of the publisher of this source using multiple lines if necessary.
Here is a new line in this field"""
		date.value.spanning {
			from {
				value.full_date 1 JAN 1980
				calendar gregorian
			}
			to {
				value.full_date 1 FEB 1982
				calendar gregorian
			}
		}
		place.place P3
		repository {
			repository R1
			locator 920.23
			remark A short note about the repository link. This note is about the repository (if more information is needed other than call number and simple description). Notes about the Source itself are usually entered elsewhere.
		}
		media M2
		note {
			text """
Comments on "Everything You Every Wanted to Know about GEDCOM Tags" SOURCE Record.

This is a set of notes about this SOURCE record. These notes are for anything else needed. There are other places to enter notes about the storage of the source (in the Repository link) and about the data in the source (in the DATA structure).

This particular SOURCE record uses all possible GEDCOM tags for a SOURCE record. Some things to check are:

1. Are the separate notes structures in the Repository link and the DATA structure preserved on importing?

2. Does the software recognize two sets of event types in the DATA structure?

3. Are the multimedia links preserved?

4. This record as two sets of notes - this one in a separate record and a second one embedded in the SOURCE record. Are they both imported and kept separate?"""
			audit.creation.date 2000-06-13T17:04:24Z
		}
		note {
			text These are notes embedded in the SOURCE Record instead of in a separate NOTE RECORD.
			audit.creation.date 2026-10-26T00:00:00Z
		}
		note {
			text """
A note about data in source.

This note includes a blank line before this text. These notes are used to describe the data in this source. Notes about the source itself are usually entered in a different set of notes."""
			audit.creation.date 2026-10-26T00:00:00Z
		}
		note {
			title Events recorded
			text """
BIRT, CHR
DEAT, FROM 1 JAN 1980 TO 1 FEB 1982, County Some, Ireland"""
			audit.creation.date 2026-10-26T00:00:00Z
		}
		note {
			title Text from source
			text """
This section is used to generic text from the course. It will usually be a quote from the text that is relevant to the use of this source in the current GEDCOM file.

It may use as many lines as needed."""
			audit.creation.date 2001-01-14T14:29:25Z
		}
		audit.creation.date 2001-01-14T14:29:25Z
		media M24
	}

	source SR2 {
		title.value All I Know About GEDCOM, I Learned on the Internet
		title {
